house of the dragon the massively  anticipated prequel to game of thrones  is going to hit our screens next year  and one of the stars of the original  series has commented on the new show's  trailer  nikolai costa waldo who played jaime  lannister in game of thrones has given  his reaction to the teaser  he said that he came away intrigued and  added i thought it was fun to see matt  smith in that world in that beautiful  white wig  and listen  i'm curious as everyone to see it  the danish actor went on to say  but it is a very different show it's his  own show i just hope it's great i hope  the success of game of thrones won't get  in the way for people when they  experience this new show  for us it took a while for people to get  into game of thrones  i remember the first season people were  saying  there are too many characters i don't  know what's going on  i don't think they have the luxury we  had  they have to start with where we were in  like season four or five  because that's what they will be  compared to  but i really hope that it's a massive  hit for them  the prequel has an interesting  foundation on which to lay its first  bricks  it follows undoubtedly the biggest tv  show in the world  but one that had a disappointing ending  on the one hand it should be less of a  challenge to improve on what came  directly before but on the other hand  game of thrones is still a beast of a  series to step into the shoes of  costa waldo rightly points out that the  show is going to have high expectations  right from the off and won't be given  the grace period to slow burn like the  early seasons of game of thrones  it's going to have the expectation of a  caged dragon in that it's going to be  expected to come out of the traps  quickly as well as scale the incredible  heights of its predecessor  but despite all this it's clear that  costa waldo is as excited as the fans  regardless of how game of thrones ended  it's clear there's a massive appetite  for house of the dragon and there's  already plenty of support for the other  prequels waiting in the wings to make a  tv airing  when house of the dragon finally makes  it to our screens next year perhaps  costa waldo will let us all know what he  thinks of the premiere
 

